KQL QUERY TO FIND OUT IF ANY USERS HAVE VISITED BOTNET, MALICIOUS, PHISHING, OR SUSPICIOUS SITES OR NOT

The query can be used for identifying possible coordinated attacks or unusual activity across multiple users within a 1-hour window. 
The activities could indicate an ongoing security threat, such as a botnet attack, phishing attempt, or other malicious activity involving multiple users.

CommonSecurityLog
| where DeviceVendor == "Zscaler"
| where DeviceProduct == "NSSWeblog"
| where DeviceEventCategory has_any ("Botnet","Malicious","Phishing","Suspicious")
| where SourceUserName contains "SOURCEUSERNAME"
| summarize StartTime = min(TimeGenerated), EndTime = max(TimeGenerated), URLCategory = make_set(DeviceEventCategory), ApplicationProtocol = make_set(ApplicationProtocol), SourceUsers = make_set(SourceUserName), DstIp = make_set(DestinationIP), FileType = make_set(FileType), URL = make_set(RequestURL), Method = make_set(RequestMethod),SrcIp = make_set(SourceTranslatedAddress),SrcIpPublic = make_set(SourceIP), SourceUserCount = dcount(SourceUserName), DstIpCount = dcount(DestinationIP), count() by DestinationHostName, bin(TimeGenerated,1h)
| where SourceUserCount > 5
| mv-expand SourceUsers
| extend SourceUsers = tostring(SourceUsers)
| summarize StartTime = min(StartTime), EndTime = max(EndTime), URLCategory = make_set(URLCategory), ApplicationProtocol = make_set(ApplicationProtocol), SourceUsers = make_set(SourceUsers), DstIp = make_set(DstIp), FileType = make_set(FileType), URL = make_set(URL), Method = make_set(Method),SrcIp = make_set(SrcIp),SrcIpPublic = make_set(SrcIpPublic), SourceUserCount = dcount(SourceUsers), count() by DestinationHostName
